  "worked_solution": "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-8,8),$ we can substitute $x=-8$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 64 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-2)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
